cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this reproducibility artifact, please cite the archived software
  release using the metadata below and cite the companion paper when available.
title: >-
  SuRT-Virtual Rwanda: reproducibility artifact for district-level
  environmental-layer preparation and provenance labelling
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tuyishime
    given-names: Audre Prince
    affiliation: Clinton Health Access Initiative
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0799-3140"
abstract: >-
  Companion software and district-level environmental layers with explicit
  per-file source and licence metadata for a Rwanda proof of concept. The
  artifact provides R and Python pipelines
  for rainfall, temperature, vegetation-greenness, and low-lying terrain
  share aggregated to Rwanda's 30 districts, together
  with a fail-closed provenance and evidence-class labelling module. It is a
  descriptive, non-operational research artifact and contains no patient,
  surveillance, or other confidential operational data.
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-07-29
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21677162"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro"
url: "https://github.com/PrinceAudre/surt-virtual-rwanda-repro"
keywords:
  - Rwanda
  - reproducible research
  - climate and health
  - geospatial analysis
  - provenance
  - public health
  - R
